  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>For the system of linear equations</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math>,</p><p>Now finding,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>5</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>&#945;</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mn>7</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>35</mn></math></p><p>Now we know that, for unique solution<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>So, in option&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>B</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;corresponds to infinitely many solution, which is completely wrong hence, this is answer.</p></blockquote>",
